{"created": "2022-07-24T14:35:24.004006+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-25T09:02:09.336156+00:00", "id": 6894273, "conceptrecid": "6894272", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6894272", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "metadata": {"title": "Global Mangrove Watch (1996 - 2020) Version 3.0 Dataset", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "publication_date": "2022-07-24", "description": "<p><strong>PLEASE BE AWARE THAT THE GMW v4.1 TIMESERIES IS NOW AVAILABLE (JULY 2026) AND THIS IS A SIGNIFICANT IMPROVEMENT OVER v3.0 AND FOR THE MAJORITY OF USERS YOU SHOULD BE USING THOSE LAYERS. THEY ARE AVAILABLE AT THE REFERENCE BELOW:</strong><br><br><strong>Bunting, P., Hilarides, L., Rosenqvist, A., Oakes, G., Castro Brand&atilde;o Vaz dos Santos, P., Worthington, T., Rosenqvist, J., Zanaga, D., Van De Kerchove, R., Tadono, T., &amp; Kobayashi, K. (2026). Global Mangrove Watch: Timeseries of Mangrove Extent (Version 4.1.12) [Data set]. Zenodo. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21346456\">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21346456</a>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This study has used L-band Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) global mosaic datasets from the Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency (JAXA) for 11 epochs from 1996 to 2020 to develop a long-term time-series of global mangrove extent and change. The study used a map-to-image approach to change detection where the baseline map (GMW v2.5) was updated using thresholding and a contextual mangrove change mask. This approach was applied between all image-date pairs producing 10 maps for each epoch, which were summarised to produce the global mangrove time-series. The resulting mangrove extent maps had an estimated accuracy of 87.4 % (95th conf. int.: 86.2 - 88.6 %), although the accuracies of the individual gain and loss change classes were lower at 58.1 % (52.4 - 63.9 %) and 60.6 % (56.1 - 64.8 %), respectively. Sources of error included a mis-registration in the SAR mosaic datasets, which could only be partially corrected for, but also confusion in fragmented areas of mangroves, such as around aquaculture ponds. Overall, 152,604 km<sup>2</sup> (133,996 -&nbsp;176,910) of mangroves were identified for 1996, with this decreasing by -5,245&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;(-13,587 -&nbsp;3686) resulting in a total extent of 147,359&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;(127,925 -&nbsp;168,895) in 2020, and representing an estimated loss of 3.4&nbsp;% over the 24-year time period. The Global Mangrove Watch Version 3.0 represents the most comprehensive record of global mangrove change achieved to date and is expected to support a wide range of activities, including the ongoing monitoring of the global coastal environment, defining and assessments of progress towards conservation targets, protected area planning and risk assessments of mangrove ecosystems worldwide.</p>\n<p>The paper which goes along with this dataset is available at the following reference:</p>\n<p>Bunting, P.; Rosenqvist, A.; Hilarides, L.; Lucas, R.M.; Thomas, T.; Tadono, T.; Worthington, T.A.; Spalding, M.; Murray, N.J.; Rebelo, L-M. Global Mangrove Extent Change 1996 &ndash; 2020: Global Mangrove Watch Version 3.0. Remote Sensing. 2022</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bunting, Pete", "affiliation": "Department Geography and Earth Sciences, Aberystwyth University, SY23 3DB, UK", "orcid": "0000-0002-7435-0148"}, {"name": "Rosenqvist, Ake", "affiliation": "solo Earth Observation (soloEO), Tokyo 104-0054, Japan", "orcid": "0000-0001-7896-502X"}, {"name": "Hilarides, Lammert", "affiliation": "Wetlands International, 6700AL Wageningen, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-4364-7547"}, {"name": "Lucas, Richard", "affiliation": "Department Geography and Earth Sciences, Aberystwyth University, SY23 3DB, UK", "orcid": "0000-0003-3010-3302"}, {"name": "Thomas, Nathan", "affiliation": "Earth System Science Interdisciplinary Research Center (ESSIC), University of Maryland, College Park, MD 20740, USA", "orcid": "0000-0002-7808-6444"}, {"name": "Tadono, Takeo", "affiliation": "Earth Observation Research Center, Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency, Tsukuba, Ibaraki 305-8505, Japan", "orcid": "0000-0003-4313-5645"}, {"name": "Worthington, Thomas", "affiliation": "Department of Zoology, University of Cambridge, The David Attenborough Building, Pembroke Street, Cambridge, CB2 3QZ, UK", "orcid": "0000-0002-8138-9075"}, {"name": "Spalding, Mark", "affiliation": "The Nature Conservancy, Siena 53100, Italy"}, {"name": "Murray, Nicholas", "affiliation": "College of Science and Engineering, James Cook University, Townsville, Queensland, Australia", "orcid": "0000-0002-4008-3053"}, {"name": "Rebelo, Lisa-Maria", "affiliation": "International Water Management Institute, 127 Sunil Mawatha, Colombo, Sri Lanka", "orcid": "0000-0002-8785-7810"}], "keywords": ["mangrove", "global", "extent", "1996", "2020", "change"], "version": "3.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "NE/P014127/1", "internal_id": "10.13039/100014013::NE/P014127/1", "funder": {"name": "UK Research and Innovation", "doi": "10.13039/100014013", "acronym": "UKRI"}, "title": "MOnitoring Mangrove ExteNT &amp; Services (MOMENTS): What is controlling Tipping Points?", "program": "NERC"}], "communities": [{"id": "globalmangrovewatch"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6894272"}}]}}, "title": "Global Mangrove Watch (1996 - 2020) Version 3.0 Dataset", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6894273", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6894273", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6894273?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6894273", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6894273/draft/pids/doi", "parent